         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Commander\n\nAs the commander of your learning, you should:\n\n- Be benevolent with yourself and with people who have not understood subtraction yet, and help them learn.\n- Be honest with yourself, and do not let your confidence underestimate or overestimate the problem ahead of you.\n- Respect yourself by remembering that there are different ways to understand math. Discover the way that makes you feel comfortable and follow it. At History Tracers, we will do our best to help you find your road.\n- Use your wisdom to identify your weaknesses, so you can train them and turn them into strengths.\n- Use your sincerity to see where you need to improve, and do not build barriers because of the difficulties you may find.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
